{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-source-safety","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's highest-risk change is the source-safe refactor of write-session-env.sh; BASH_SOURCE guard placement, return-vs-exit in the helper, and errexit isolation from implement-bootstrap.sh are subtle shell-execution semantics that general correctness reviewers typically miss.","prompt_body":"Review the proposed source-safe refactor of scripts/write-session-env.sh: verify the BASH_SOURCE guard correctly scopes set -euo pipefail, lib-quiet init, and argument parsing to argv0 only, so sourcing the file into implement-bootstrap.sh does not inject errexit into that parent shell (which runs set -uo pipefail without -e). Check that emit_plugin_root_env uses return 0 on skip and invalid-value paths rather than exit, since implement-bootstrap.sh sources the helper and an exit call would abort the resume-tail branch mid-run. Verify the plan's ordering guarantee holds for cold-start: that plugin-root.env is emitted by session-setup.sh before any post-Step-0 Bash block sources it, and that the resume-tail sync in implement-bootstrap.sh fires before the first post-Step-0 block needing the file in a legacy-resume run. Check that the pre-bootstrap two-line form (source+awk, then unconditional export) actually resolves CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT on first contact when plugin-root.env is absent from a legacy resume tmpdir, and whether the unconditional export after the awk line preserves behavioral equivalence with the old four-line form that also exported unconditionally. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"count-assertion-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan asserts specific fence counts (37 post-Step-0 + 3 pre-bootstrap + 1 prose = 41; awk-fallback exactly 3; old if-fence exactly 0 post-edit) and maps them directly to test grep assertions; if those counts are wrong relative to what SKILL.md actually contains, or the test strings do not match the post-edit form, the CI gate silently vacuously passes while no longer covering rehydration.","prompt_body":"Read skills/implement/SKILL.md and count total occurrences of the exact four-line awk fence opener to verify the plan's claimed 41 executable sites minus 1 prose example; check whether the three pre-bootstrap sites the plan names at approximate lines 105-108, 307-311, and 466-469 are actually distinct from the 37 post-Step-0 sites and not adjacent to other fences that could cause a line-number drift error during mechanical replacement. Read scripts/test-implement-timing-rehydration.sh around lines 78-132 and verify that the plan's proposed new assertions (guarded-source-line count equals 41, awk-extract count equals 3, old if-fence opener count equals 0) use grep match strings that will exactly match the post-edit SKILL.md text rather than accidentally matching in comments, prose, or the prelude documentation block. Check whether Invariant C's proposed new detector for the one-line source form uses a string anchored tightly enough to distinguish the post-Step-0 source-only line from the pre-bootstrap source+awk form, so the count of 37 vs 3 is assertable separately if needed. Verify the write-session-env.md documentation update in the plan correctly reflects the skip conditions (empty value and /dev/null output) that the test-session-env-roundtrip.sh assertions will exercise. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
